## 2. Top-level fields (19)

`R` = always required · `C` = conditionally required · `O` = optional

| # | Field | Req | Type | Invariants |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `schema_version` | R | `{"const":"1.0.0"}` | must equal `$id`'s version segment (§6.1 self-test) |
| 2 | `id` | R | `$ref: node_id` | — |
| 3 | `kind` | R | `{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-z_]+$"}` | `INV-ID-1`: must equal `id`'s middle segment → **L2** (cross-field string compare) |
| 4 | `status` | R | `$ref: status` | `INV-DEL-1`: no `DELETED` member |
| 5 | `content` | R | `{"type":"object","minProperties":1}` | opaque (A2); an empty payload is a node asserting nothing |
| 6 | `content_hash` | R | `$ref: sha256` | `INV-HASH-1`: `= sha256(JCS(content))` → **L2** (recompute) |
| 7 | `created_at` | R | `$ref: timestamp` | — |
| 8 | `updated_at` | R | `$ref: timestamp` | `INV-TIME-1`: `>= created_at` → **L2** (compare) |
| 9 | `provenance` | R | `$ref: provenance` | §5 |
| 10 | `confidence` | R | `$ref: confidence` | §3 |
| 11 | `evidence_refs` | R | `{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"evidence_ref"},"uniqueItems":true}` | `INV-EV-1`: `minItems: 1` unless `status == PROPOSED` (A11) |
| 12 | `promotion` | C | `$ref: promotion` | `INV-PROMO-3`: required iff `status != PROPOSED`; forbidden when `status == PROPOSED` |
| 13 | `derived_from` | O | array of `node_id`, `uniqueItems` | `INV-LIN-1`: all resolve, no cycle → **L2** |
| 14 | `trust_zone` | R | `$ref: trust_zone` | `INV-TZ-1`: `Z0` requires `provenance.actor_role == "founder"` (only the founder may author into the sealed layer, `constitution/README.md:3`) |
| 15 | `labels` | O | `{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"type":"string"},"propertyNames":{"pattern":"^[a-z][a-z0-9_.]*$"}}` | free-form; the one deliberately open field, so producers have an escape valve that does not require schema amendment |
| 16 | `superseded_by` | C | `$ref: node_id` | `INV-DEL-2`: required iff `status == SUPERSEDED`; forbidden otherwise |
| 17 | `retraction` | C | `$ref: retraction` | `INV-DEL-3`: required iff `status == RETRACTED`; forbidden otherwise |
| 18 | `quarantine` | C | `$ref: quarantine` | `INV-QUAR-1`: required iff `status == QUARANTINED`; forbidden otherwise |
| 19 | `deprecation` | C | `$ref: deprecation` | `INV-DEP-1`: required iff `status == DEPRECATED`; forbidden otherwise |

Top level carries **`"unevaluatedProperties": false`** — `INV-DEL-4` (rejects a `deleted: true`
flag) and the general closed-world guarantee. Not `additionalProperties` (`design.md` §2.5.1).

### 2.1 The lifecycle-detail family (16-19)

Fields 16-19 are mutually exclusive and jointly determined by `status`. The **iff** in each
invariant is deliberate: the `then` branch requires the matching block and the `else` branch
*forbids* it, so a node can neither omit the block its status demands nor carry one its status
contradicts (`design.md` §5.4 D5). Four parallel `allOf` members, one per block:

```jsonc
{
  "$comment": "INV-DEL-3: RETRACTED iff tombstone present; no node leaves the graph silently",
  "if":   { "properties": { "status": { "const": "RETRACTED" } }, "required": ["status"] },
  "then": { "required": ["retraction"] },
  "else": { "not": { "required": ["retraction"] } }
}
```

> The `"required": ["status"]` inside `if` is not redundant. Without it, an instance *missing*
> `status` vacuously satisfies the `if` and gets pushed down the `then` branch, producing a
> confusing cascade of errors instead of one clean `required: status` failure. Apply this to all
> four clauses and to the promotion clause (field 12).

