## 3. `confidence` — derived, never authored

```jsonc
"confidence": {
  "$comment": "INV-CONF-1: confidence is a derivation record, never an authored scalar",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["value", "method", "inputs", "computed_at", "computed_by"],
  "properties": {
    "value":       { "$comment": "INV-CONF-5: a confidence outside [0,1] is not a probability",
                     "type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1 },
    "method":      { "$ref": "#/$defs/confidence_method",
                     "$comment": "INV-CONF-2: no authored/asserted member exists" },
    "inputs":      { "$comment": "INV-CONF-3: a derivation with no inputs is authoring in disguise",
                     "type": "array", "minItems": 1, "uniqueItems": true,
                     "items": { "anyOf": [ {"$ref":"#/$defs/evidence_ref"},
                                           {"$ref":"#/$defs/node_id"} ] } },
    "computed_at": { "$ref": "#/$defs/timestamp" },
    "computed_by": { "$comment": "INV-CONF-4: a component computed this, not a person",
                     "type": "string", "pattern": "^sakg\\.confidence\\.[a-z_]+$" }
  },
  "unevaluatedProperties": false
}
```

`confidence_method` enum — all four name a *procedure*:

| Method | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `court_ratified` | The Verification Court's verdict set the value |
| `evidence_weighted` | Computed from the weights of `inputs` |
| `ancestor_min` | `min()` over `derived_from` — a derived claim is no more certain than its weakest premise |
| `decay_adjusted` | A prior value aged by a time-decay model |

There is no `authored`, `asserted`, `estimated`, or `expert_judgement` member, and adding one is the
single edit that would disarm `INV-CONF-2`. A founder judgement enters as a `court_ratified` value
whose `inputs` cite the ratification node — the judgement becomes evidence rather than bypassing it.

**Even a `PROPOSED` node has ≥1 input.** Its confidence derives from its own provenance record (the
run that produced it), so `inputs: ["sakg:evidence:<the provenance attestation>"]`. This keeps
`minItems: 1` unconditional, which is what makes `INV-CONF-3` a hard rule rather than a
status-dependent one.

