## 4. `promotion` — evidence-gated, never frequency-gated

```jsonc
"promotion": {
  "$comment": "INV-PROMO-2: every transition is evidenced and epistemically based; INV-PROMO-4: no property beyond this set — blocks a smuggled observation_count",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["from", "to", "at", "basis", "evidence_refs", "actor"],
  "properties": {
    "from":  { "$ref": "#/$defs/status" },
    "to":    { "$ref": "#/$defs/status" },
    "at":    { "$ref": "#/$defs/timestamp" },
    "basis": { "$ref": "#/$defs/basis",
               "$comment": "INV-PROMO-1: basis is epistemic; no count is a basis" },
    "evidence_refs": { "type": "array", "minItems": 1, "uniqueItems": true,
                       "items": { "$ref": "#/$defs/evidence_ref" } },
    "actor": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "note":  { "type": "string" }
  },
  "unevaluatedProperties": false,
  "allOf": [ { "$ref": "#/$defs/legal_transition" },
             /* … basis↔transition binding clauses, INV-FSM-2 … */ ]
}
```

`basis` enum (8):

| Basis | Meaning | Legal on |
|---|---|---|
| `deterministic_evidence` | A reproducible command produced the claimed result (the `CANARY-0001` mechanism, `constitution/canaries/README.md:40-42`) | promotion edges |
| `court_ratification` | The Verification Court ruled | promotion edges, `ACTIVE→DEPRECATED` |
| `adversary_cleared` | The Adversary reviewed a quarantine and found no defect | `QUARANTINED→*` |
| `founder_ratification` | Human override | every edge |
| `supersession` | A named replacement exists | `*→SUPERSEDED`, `ACTIVE→DEPRECATED` |
| `falsification` | The claim was shown false | `*→RETRACTED` |
| `integrity_alarm` | Evidence or provenance is suspect; truth undetermined | `*→QUARANTINED` |
| `evidence_withdrawn` | Supporting evidence was itself retracted | `CANDIDATE→PROPOSED` |

**No member is a count.** `frequency`, `observation_count`, `consensus_count`, `repetition`,
`seen_n_times` are all absent, and `unevaluatedProperties: false` means none of them can ride along
as a sibling property either. The two defences are independent by construction
(`design.md` §5.3).

> **A near-miss worth recording.** "N independent ratifiers agreed" looks count-shaped. It is
> modelled as `court_ratification` with N entries in `evidence_refs`, *not* as a numeric threshold
> field. The distinction that matters: each ratification is an addressable, retractable artifact,
> whereas a tally is not — you cannot retract a number. If a ratification is later found forged
> (`CANARY-0001`), the promotion that leaned on it is traceable through `evidence_refs`. A counter
> would have erased that link. (`assumptions.md` A5.)

