## 6. Lifecycle detail blocks

All four carry `unevaluatedProperties: false`.

```jsonc
"retraction": {
  "$comment": "the tombstone: deletion is only expressible as a retraction with attribution",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["reason", "retracted_at", "retracted_by", "evidence_refs"],
  "properties": {
    "reason":        { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "retracted_at":  { "$ref": "#/$defs/timestamp" },
    "retracted_by":  { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "evidence_refs": { "type": "array", "minItems": 1, "uniqueItems": true,
                       "items": { "$ref": "#/$defs/evidence_ref" } },
    "successor":     { "$ref": "#/$defs/node_id" }
  },
  "unevaluatedProperties": false
},

"quarantine": {
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["reason", "raised_at", "raised_by", "detector"],
  "properties": {
    "reason":    { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "raised_at": { "$ref": "#/$defs/timestamp" },
    "raised_by": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "detector":  { "$comment": "which detector fired — mirrors the canary detection_signature convention",
                   "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "canary_id": { "type": "string", "pattern": "^CANARY-\\d{4}$" }
  },
  "unevaluatedProperties": false
},

"deprecation": {
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["reason", "deprecated_at"],
  "properties": {
    "reason":         { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "deprecated_at":  { "$ref": "#/$defs/timestamp" },
    "prefer_instead": { "$ref": "#/$defs/node_id" }
  },
  "unevaluatedProperties": false
}
```

`retraction.evidence_refs` has `minItems: 1`: you may not retract a node on a hunch, for the same
reason you may not promote one on a hunch. `quarantine` has **no** evidence requirement — raising a
quarantine is a *suspicion*, and requiring proof to raise one would suppress exactly the alarms the
`CANARY` corpus exists to trigger (`constitution/canaries/README.md:5-6`: a miss "is an alarm").
`quarantine.canary_id` lets a calibration miss point at the specific canary, matching the corpus's
"a miss points at the exact detector to fix" intent (`constitution/canaries/README.md:28-29`).

